; The slow tier: tests that run only with PRIGH_TEST_TIER=full (`./test
; --full`), the ones taking about 100ms of CPU or 1s of wall or more (git,
; subprocesses, servers, timers), in test/full/ and test/terminal/. Their
; inline_tests are (enabled_if (= %{env:PRIGH_TEST_TIER=default} full)): the
; libraries build in every run, so they never fall behind the cheap tests
; whose helpers they open. test/full/test_x_full.ml holds test/test_x.ml's
; slow tests; test_x.ml keeps the cheap ones, so every area still has tests in
; the default run. @runtest type-checks them too, for `dune build @runtest` by
; hand.

(rule
 (alias runtest)
 (deps
  (alias test/full/check)
  (alias test/terminal/check))
 (action (progn)))
